          "meaning": "to Janaka",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": 4
        },
        {
          "itrans": "niriikshitum",
          "iast": "nirīkśitum",
          "devanagari": "निरीक्शितुं",
          "meaning": "to gaze at [have the face]",
          "anvayaIndex": 4,
          "verseIndex": 11
        },
        {
          "itrans": "katham shakshe",
          "iast": "katham śakśe",
          "devanagari": "कथं शक्शे",
          "meaning": "how, I am capable [how can I stand.]",
          "anvayaIndex": 5,
          "verseIndex": 9
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "3.62.13",
      "label": "3.62.13",
      "numbers": [
        13
      ],
      "devanagari": "विदेह रजो नूनम् माम् दृष्ट्वा विरहितम् तया\nसुता विनाश संतप्तो मोहस्य वशम् एष्यति |",
      "iast": "videha rajo nūnam mām dṛṣṭvā virahitam tayā\nsutā vināśa santapto mohasya vaśam eṣyati |",
      "translation": "\"On seeing me without Seetha the king of Videha will be distraught by the perishing of his daughter, and he defiantly goes under the preponderance of perplexity...",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "videha rajaH",
          "iast": "videha rajaḥ",
          "devanagari": "विदेह रजः",
