          "iast": "mohasya vaśam eṣyati",
          "devanagari": "मोहस्य वशं एष्यति",
          "meaning": "of perplexity, preponderance, goes under",
          "anvayaIndex": 4,
          "verseIndex": 10
        },
        {
          "itrans": "nuunam",
          "iast": "nūnam",
          "devanagari": "नूनं",
          "meaning": "it is definite.",
          "anvayaIndex": 5,
          "verseIndex": 2
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "3.62.14",
      "label": "3.62.14",
      "numbers": [
        14
      ],
      "devanagari": "अथवा न गमिष्यामि पुरीम् भरत पालितम्\nस्वर्गो अपि हि तया हीनः शून्य एव मतो मम |",
      "iast": "athavā na gamiṣyāmi purīm bharata pālitam\nsvargo api hi tayā hīnaḥ śūnya eva mato mama |",
      "translation": "\"Instead, I prefer not to go to the city Ayodhya that is ruled by Bharata, because it must be comforting to one and all under his rulership, but not to me as Seetha will not be with me... else if, that end of my life occurs now and if I were to go to heaven, even that heaven will be a void to me without her... I believe so...",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "athavaa",
          "iast": "athavā",
          "devanagari": "अथवा",
          "meaning": "instead",
